From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpu: mali-valhall-csf: add MT6897

The Mali-G615 of the MediaTek MT6897 is integrated like the G925 of the
MT8196: power, clocks and the OPP table come from the
mediatek,mt6897-gpufreq power domain, and so does the mask of working
shader cores.

There is no need for a compatible of its own in the driver, the generic
one does. MT8196 is special there for its ASN hash, and the vendor
kernel doesn't use one for MT6897: its device tree has no
l2-hash-values, the only way to set it in the Mali driver.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml        | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
index 8eccd43..5839374 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/arm,mali-valhall-csf.yaml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ properties:
     oneOf:
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - mediatek,mt6897-mali      # G615
               - mediatek,mt8196-mali
               - nxp,imx95-mali            # G310
               - rockchip,rk3588-mali
@@ -127,7 +128,9 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           contains:
-            const: mediatek,mt8196-mali
+            enum:
+              - mediatek,mt6897-mali
+              - mediatek,mt8196-mali
     then:
       properties:
         mali-supply: false
